{
  "message": "I can help. Your order #W4923227 is pending, so payment changes can be made on a pending order using the available order-modification process. I’m not certain from the supplied policy whether a partial gift-card balance can be applied to an existing pending order; the available action is to switch the payment method rather than split payment. Your gift card balance is $60.00, while the order total is $321.18, so I can’t confidently apply it to cover the whole order.

I do see a Visa on your account: credit_card_8897086, ending in 8902. Would you like me to switch order #W4923227 to that Visa? Please reply yes or no.

Sources: retail/policy.md:retail-agent-policy-domain-basic-order, retail/policy.md:retail-agent-policy-generic-action-rules"
}

{"message":"I found the matching delivered order, #W7181492. It includes the Garden Hose, Backpack, and Hiking Boots you mentioned.

I also found the waterproof version of the same Hiking Boots product in the same size/material: size 12, leather, waterproof: yes, item 8277474082. It’s available, and it costs $236.57 versus $260.56 for your original boots, so there would be a $23.99 refund difference if exchanged.

However, I’m not able to complete both a return and an exchange on the same delivered order with the available self-service tools, because delivered-order return/exchange actions can only be done once per order. I’ve transferred this to a human agent with the order and item details so they can help resolve the combined return and exchange request."}

{
  "message": "I can help with the payment change. Order #W4923227 is currently pending, and pending orders can be modified; I checked the order status first as required for order actions. Source: retail/policy.md:retail-agent-policy-domain-basic-order

For applying the $60 gift card balance to this existing order: I don’t have an available tool to apply a partial gift card balance to an already-placed order, so I’m not certain that can be done through this support flow.

I can change the payment method for pending order #W4923227 from your Mastercard ending in 4336 to your Visa ending in 8902, using payment method credit_card_8897086. Please confirm: do you want me to change the payment method on order #W4923227 to the Visa ending in 8902?"
}

{
  "message": "Done — I changed the payment method on order #W4923227 to your Visa ending in 8902.\n\nThe order is still pending. The payment history now shows a new $321.18 payment on the Visa and a $321.18 refund back to the Mastercard ending in 4336."
}

{
  "message": "I can help with that, Amelia. To look up your account and review your orders, could you please provide the email address on your account? If you don’t remember it, I can look you up using your first name, last name, and ZIP code instead."
}

{
  "message": "I found your account under amelia.silva7872@example.com. I can review the orders on the account and help cancel any that are still pending, and for delivered orders I can help set up returns. I’ll need to check each order’s status first because orders can only be cancelled if they’re pending, and returns can only be requested for delivered orders [retail/policy.md:retail-agent-policy-cancel-pending-order; retail/policy.md:retail-agent-policy-return-delivered-order].\n\nI found these orders on your account: #W2586676, #W5400801, #W4597054, #W4836353, #W7773202, and #W7342738. I’ll pull up the details now so we can see what’s eligible."
}

{
  "message": "I can help with that. First I’ll need to look up the order and confirm it’s still pending, since changes can generally only be made to pending orders. Please provide either the order ID, or the email address on the account. Also, please tell me which items you’d like to change and what options you want instead. If you want the order sent to your usual/default address, I can look that up once I identify the account."
}

{
  "message": "I can help look into those order changes. To find your account, could you please provide the email address on the account? If you don’t remember it, I can search by your first name, last name, and ZIP code instead."
